velopment, the defences were multivallate with a timber palisade [1]. Later, a bank was built over the line of the palisade, replacing it [1]. The fort is large and encloses an area of 10.5 hectares [1]. Miscellaneous finds at Caesar''s Camp include a Roman roof tile, which is now held in Camberley Museum, and an early rapier dating to the Middle Bronze Age (c. 1500–1000 BC) [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95181", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95182", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302103", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
