rs of a farm; a generally old building without roof, only with walls) is an archaeological site in Bolivia [1]. It is located in the Cochabamba Department, Quillacollo Province, Sipe Sipe Municipality, near the community of Linku [1]. Inka Raqay was declared a National Archaeological Monument by Law No. 3479 of September 22, 2006 [1]. By Law No. 295 of September 28, 2012, it was declared a Historical and Cultural Heritage of the Bolivian state [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99996", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99997", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''1400'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99998", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:141472", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-01a_fields-wd3-s001: site_type None -> ''Ruin''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150939", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5d0819e0/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5d0819e0/Ruinas de Inka Raqay.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302131", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''1000 - 1500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302132", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''1460''"}]'::jsonb),
