e Welsh Way exists today as a named lane which leaves the Gloucester-Cirencester road before Duntisbourne and passes through Barnsley and Ready Token to Fairford and Lechlade [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101848", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101849", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153820", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-017: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/The_Welsh_Way_-_geograph.org.uk_-_296535.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7c097275/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250157", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250158", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
