    ('89bdbe2c-a19b-484d-b6ef-2ed464b1311b'::uuid, 'mystery', '9', '8', 'card-stats-2026-10-04b-rollback:89bdbe2c-a19b-484d-b6ef-2ed464b1311b:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-10-04b: mystery ''8'' restored on Chaa Creek', '4c0777f27d6529943e7bcc36bbf08121', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 9 from (''Settlement'', None) is shared by 2 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export a991f0242bf4f80c (2026-10-04 18:08:44.180088+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 133 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59724 cells (basis: wave 2026-10-04''s own export (2026-10-04 13:55:46.282309+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81066", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2018:chunk-0001: description ''Chaa Creek is a tributary of the Macal River in the Cayo District of western Belize, with Maya ruins that remain largely unexcavated in its catchment basin. In 1997, a survey led by Anabel Ford of Harvard University employed ground-penetrating radar and surface surveys, identifying over 20 unexcavated structures in and near the Chaa Creek area. The site encompasses over 70 recorded archaeological features within a 500-acre area, including structural mounds indicative of residential areas and agricultural terraces adapted to the riverine landscape. Chaa Creek is posited to be a satellite settlement of Xunantunich, the major Maya ceremonial centre nearby that peaked around 600-900 AD with a population of some 10,000 people.'' -> ''Chaa Creek is a tributary of the Macal River in the Cayo District in western Belize [1]. It is near the site of an ancient Maya settlement [1]. Initial investigation and surveying of the site was done from 1992 to 1994 under the auspices of the Xunantunich Archaelogical Project [1]. Excavations were conducted in 1995 and 1997 [1]. Significant pottery finds and other artifacts have been recovered at the site, which is posited to be a satellite site of Xunantunich [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120304", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120305", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''-200'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120306", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaa_Creek'' -> ''https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=18170''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155284", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/89bdbe2c/hero.webp'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
