ntury indicate that the cave was later occupied by Neanderthals during the late Middle Paleolithic (likely sometime roughly around 60-40,000 years ago) [1]. A prehistoric upper jawbone fragment of a modern human was discovered in the cavern during a 1927 excavation by the Torquay Natural History Society and named Kents Cavern 4 [1]. The cave was where the holotype canine teeth of the sabertooth cat Homotherium latidens were collected by John MacEnery in 1826, and formally described by Richard Owen in 1846 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104192", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104193", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-500000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156017", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/931ddb0f/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/931ddb0f/Kents Cavern (6990).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302163", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:302164", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04a_fields-wd4-s001: period_start None -> ''-2580000''"}]'::jsonb),
